---
Add waveform oscilloscope display.

Show real-time waveform visualization of the audio output or selected
track's output in a small panel.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Oscilloscope panel shows current audio waveform
- [ ] Updates at display frame rate (not audio rate)
- [ ] Waveform is stable (trigger-based display, not free-running)
- [ ] Ring buffer captures audio data for display without blocking audio thread
- [ ] Reasonable CPU usage (<1% for visualization)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Play audio, verify waveform displayed
- [ ] Verify waveform matches expected shape (sine = smooth, drum = transient)
- [ ] Stop playback, verify display goes flat
- [ ] Verify no audio glitches caused by visualization
